<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs end firmer in N.Y., Dow rises 50.68 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs end firmer in N.Y., Dow rises 50.68 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs ended firmer while the Dow Jones Index rose 50.68 points to 5,889.20.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S. and Britain.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$22 3/4	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$24 1/8	 nil</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 1/4	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13 7/8	 nil</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$76 7/8	 +0 3/4</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  35		  +0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  231 1/2	   +1</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col London  158 3/4	   +1 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  135 1/4	   +1 3/4</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
